## 📌 Project Overview & Business Problem

Understanding **who your customers are** is the foundation of any effective retention, marketing, or personalization strategy. Most e-commerce businesses treat every customer identically — sending the same promotions to a first-time buyer and a loyal repeat purchaser — which leads to wasted marketing spend and missed retention opportunities.

This project solves that problem by building an **RFM (Recency, Frequency, Monetary) based customer segmentation model** on raw e-commerce transaction data. Using unsupervised machine learning (**K-Means Clustering**), customers are grouped into distinct, actionable segments — enabling targeted marketing, churn prevention, and revenue optimization strategies.

> 💡 **Business Value:** Instead of guessing which customers to prioritize, this pipeline delivers data-backed customer personas (e.g., *Loyal High-Spenders*, *At-Risk Customers*, *Recent New Buyers*) that stakeholders can act on immediately.

---

## ✨ Key Features

- 🧹 **Automated Data Cleaning Pipeline** — Handles missing values, filters incomplete/cancelled orders, and parses transaction dates.
- 📊 **RFM Feature Engineering** — Calculates Recency, Frequency, and Monetary metrics per customer from raw invoice-level data.
- 🔄 **Log Transformation & Standardization** — Normalizes skewed RFM distributions using `log1p` and `StandardScaler` for clustering readiness.
- 🎯 **Optimal Cluster Selection (Elbow Method)** — Determines the ideal number of customer segments using inertia curves.
- 🧠 **K-Means Clustering Engine** — Segments customers into meaningful, statistically distinct groups.
- 📈 **Rich Visual Analytics** — Scatter plots (Recency vs. Monetary, Frequency vs. Monetary) and bar charts for cluster distribution.
- 🧾 **Cluster Profiling Summary** — Aggregated statistics (mean Recency, Frequency, Monetary, and customer count) per segment for business interpretation.

---

## 🛠️ Tech Stack & Architecture

| Layer | Tools & Libraries |
|---|---|
| **Language** | Python 3.10+ |
| **Data Manipulation** | Pandas, NumPy |
| **Machine Learning** | Scikit-learn (`KMeans`, `StandardScaler`) |
| **Visualization** | Matplotlib, Seaborn |
| **Environment** | Jupyter Notebook / Google Colab |
| **Data Source** | E-commerce Transactional Dataset (`.csv`) |

### 🏗️ Pipeline Architecture

```text
Raw Transaction Data (CSV)
        │
        ▼
Data Cleaning & Filtering (Order Status = Completed)
        │
        ▼
RFM Metric Computation (Recency, Frequency, Monetary)
        │
        ▼
Log Transform + Standard Scaling
        │
        ▼
Elbow Method → Optimal K Selection
        │
        ▼
K-Means Clustering (k = 4)
        │
        ▼
Cluster Visualization & Business Profiling
```

